          "whyItBreaks": "The diff deletes the second checkout of frankekn/needlefish@main and the separate `target` checkout, then leaves only the PR-head checkout (43-47) installed (49-51) and executed as the tool (53-59) under `GH_TOKEN: secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN` with `pull-requests: write` + `checks: write` (16-19) on a self-hosted runner (23). The PR being reviewed is therefore the code doing the review: a same-repo branch (the only PRs allowed by line 24) can edit src/cli.ts to auto-approve, alter/forge another PR's check run, or exfiltrate the token, and `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` on the PR head additionally executes PR-controlled package lifecycle scripts that the old workflow never ran (the old Install step ran only in the trusted `needlefish` directory). The removed comment stated the exact property being lost: 'This prevents a PR from controlling its own review by modifying the tool.' Self-review is still achievable without this exposure by running the trusted main tool against the PR head as the target, which is what the removed pattern did."
        }
