          "lineStart": 43,
          "lineEnd": 59,
          "title": "Do not run the PR's own tool as its reviewer",
          "whyItBreaks": "The removed step checked out `frankekn/needlefish@main` into `path: needlefish` and ran the trusted tool against the PR head (`path: target`). The new workflow deletes that isolation: it checks the PR head out at the workspace root (line 43-47), runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` on the PR-controlled `package.json`/lifecycle scripts (line 49-51), and then executes `./node_modules/.bin/tsx src/cli.ts` from that same checkout while injecting `GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}` under `permissions: pull-requests: write, checks: write` (line 53-59). A same-repo PR can therefore modify `src/cli.ts` (or a package install script) so the reviewer always reports PASS, posts a forged approving review, or exfiltrates the write-scoped token — the change under review now controls the review gate. The `if:` at line 24 only restricts the `pull_request` path (fork PRs) but is short-circuited by `github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'`, so a maintainer-triggered review of a fork PR would also execute untrusted head code. This is exactly the self-reference the deleted comment protected against ('prevents a PR from controlling its own review by modifying the tool')."
        }
